### ==============================================================================
### Digital Banking System - Demonstration HTTP Requests
### ==============================================================================
### Use in IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client or VS Code REST Client.
### Ensure the application is running: ./mvnw spring-boot:run
### ==============================================================================

@host = http://localhost:8080
@adminId = 1

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. Register Customers
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Register Customer Alice (assigned ID 2 on fresh start)
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Alice Smith",
  "email": "alice@bank.com",
  "phone": "+380501234567",
  "address": "123 Main Street, Kyiv"
}

### 1.2 Register Customer Bob (assigned ID 3 on fresh start)
POST {{host}}/api/customers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "fullName": "Bob Jones",
  "email": "bob@bank.com",
  "phone": "+380509876543",
  "address": "456 Oak Avenue, Lviv"
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. Open Accounts (Factory Method & Strategy & Observer)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Open Checking Account for Alice (Factory: CheckingAccountFactory, Strategy: FixedFeeStrategy)
### Initial deposit: 500.00 EUR. System fee account gets created at startup (ID 1, CHK-SYSTEM-FEE).
POST {{host}}/api/accounts
X-User-Id: 2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerId": 2,
  "type": "CHECKING",
  "initialDeposit": 500.00
}

### 2.2 Open Savings Account for Bob (Factory: SavingsAccountFactory, Strategy: PercentageFeeStrategy)
### Initial deposit: 200.00 EUR.
POST {{host}}/api/accounts
X-User-Id: 3
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerId": 3,
  "type": "SAVINGS",
  "initialDeposit": 200.00
}

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. Check Initial Balances
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 Check Alice's Initial Balance (Expected: 500.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/2/balance
X-User-Id: 2

### 3.2 Check Bob's Initial Balance (Expected: 200.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/3/balance
X-User-Id: 3

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. Successful Transfer (Chain of Responsibility + Strategy + Observer)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 Transfer 100 EUR from Alice (Checking) to Bob (Savings)
### Checking fixed fee = 1.00 EUR.
### Total debited from Alice: 101.00 EUR. Credited to Bob: 100.00 EUR. Bank fee account: +1.00 EUR.
POST {{host}}/api/transactions/transfer
X-User-Id: 2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": 2,
  "targetAccountId": 3,
  "amount": 100.00
}

### 4.2 Verify Alice's Balance after Transfer (Expected: 399.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/2/balance
X-User-Id: 2

### 4.3 Verify Bob's Balance after Transfer (Expected: 300.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/3/balance
X-User-Id: 3

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. Rejected Transfer (Chain of Responsibility: SufficientFundsHandler)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Transfer 1000 EUR from Alice to Bob (Fails: balance 399.00 < 1001.00)
### Returns HTTP 200 with status: "REJECTED" and clear business reason.
POST {{host}}/api/transactions/transfer
X-User-Id: 2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": 2,
  "targetAccountId": 3,
  "amount": 1000.00
}

### 5.2 Verify Alice's Balance is Unchanged (Expected: 399.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/2/balance
X-User-Id: 2

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 6. Admin Waives Fees (Runtime Strategy Swap & Observer)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 6.1 Admin waives fees on Alice's Checking Account
### Swaps FixedFeeStrategy -> NoFeeStrategy; publishes FEE_POLICY_CHANGED
POST {{host}}/api/accounts/2/waive-fees
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}

### 6.2 View Alice's Account details (feeStrategy is now "NoFeeStrategy")
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/2
X-User-Id: 2

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 7. Second Transfer with Waived Fee (0.00 Fee)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 7.1 Transfer 100 EUR from Alice to Bob again (Fee: 0.00 EUR)
### Alice debited: 100.00 EUR. Bob credited: 100.00 EUR.
POST {{host}}/api/transactions/transfer
X-User-Id: 2
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": 2,
  "targetAccountId": 3,
  "amount": 100.00
}

### 7.2 Verify Alice's Final Balance (Expected: 299.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/2/balance
X-User-Id: 2

### 7.3 Verify Bob's Final Balance (Expected: 400.00 EUR)
GET {{host}}/api/accounts/3/balance
X-User-Id: 3

### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
### 8. Notifications and Audit Monitoring (Observer Pattern)
### ------------------------------------------------------------------------------

### 8.1 View Alice's Notifications (Account opened, transfer sent, transfer rejected, fees waived, transfer sent)
GET {{host}}/api/notifications?customerId=2
X-User-Id: 2

### 8.2 Mark Alice's first notification as read
PUT {{host}}/api/notifications/1/read
X-User-Id: 2

### 8.3 View Bob's Notifications (Account opened, transfers received)
GET {{host}}/api/notifications?customerId=3
X-User-Id: 3

### 8.4 View Transaction History for Alice's Account
GET {{host}}/api/transactions/history/2
X-User-Id: 2

### 8.5 Admin views System Audit Log (Recorded by AuditLogObserver)
GET {{host}}/api/audit-log
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}

### 8.6 Admin Searches all Transactions across the Bank
POST {{host}}/api/transactions/search
X-User-Id: {{adminId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "status": null
}
